WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.501
-Our next guest
is a very funny comedian

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.737
and correspondent
on "The Daily Show,"

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:06.038
which returns from hiatus
January 17th.

00:00:06.038 --> 00:00:09.241
Please welcome back to the show
Roy Wood Jr., everybody!

00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:11.377
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:16.883 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:22.422 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.490
-Yeah!
-Welcome back, Roy.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.259
-Yeah!
-Happy New Year.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.694
I want to start --
-How you been, man?

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.462
-I've been good.
I'm ready for this year.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.397
-Alright. Me too, I think.
I don't know.

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:32.899
We're only a couple days
into the [bleep]

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.167
So we'll see.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.869
-Probably too early to tell.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.536
-Yeah, yeah.
Way too early.

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:39.272
You know, I just wrapped up
the holidays, man.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.473
So I'm still, like, in a fog.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.541
-I know you got a 6-year-old.

00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:44.344
Did you have a good Christmas
with your 6-year-old?

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.345
-Christmas was good
'cause he's finally aware

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:47.646
of who gets the gifts for him.

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:49.349
-Oh, okay.
Meaning?

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:50.517
-It's good.
He's 6.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.685
He can understand now,
which is why, like,

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.021
you can never give Santa Claus
credit for the big gifts.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.222
-Okay.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.757
-Big gift, that's me,
your daddy, your mama.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.358
We got you --
You like that? Yeah.

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:00.894
That's us.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:02.094
-Okay.

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:03.729
-Sweater, the toothpaste,
that's the white dude.

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:05.731
The white dude --

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:07.300
-You call him the white dude?

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.602
-White dude.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.304
He's a black child.
I got to let him know.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.306
Sometimes them white dudes,
they gonna come in the house.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:16.042
They gonna help you
with your teeth.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.811
But, yeah, it was cool, man.
It was a good holiday.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.446
-Did you travel?

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:23.149
-No, no.
That I did not do.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.684
-Okay.
Any regrets?

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:27.586
-Well, no, after what I saw
what happened with Southwest,

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:31.824
I am happy I stayed my ass
at the house.

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.659
The thing that
I don't understand

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:35.694
about air travel, man,
is just --

00:01:35.694 --> 00:01:37.130
Like, I just really wish, like,

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.531
whenever there's, like,
a huge shutdown,

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.366
like, there's a huge storm
and there's a shutdown

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.867
and everybody's sleeping
at the airport

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:44.103
and people laying all out
in the baggage claim,

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:47.673
laying on
the baggage revolver...

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:51.610
shouldn't there just be
one airline that just says,

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.479
"[Bleep] it.
Let's try."

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:55.482
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:58.250
Like, "Let's go."

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.152
Like, there should be
one airline

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:02.655
that just be like,
"Hey, if you want to risk it...

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.491
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.625
...let's go,"
'cause I would imagine

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:08.627
there were people in the airport
who would have been --

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:10.830
What the plane hold,
about 300 people?

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.632
Find another 200,
300 people at the gate.

00:02:13.632 --> 00:02:15.634
"Hey, do you want to go?

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.469
You want to go?

00:02:17.469 --> 00:02:19.105
Let's go."

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.506
And you understand the risk.

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:21.807
It's like when you go
to Best Buy

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:23.776
and you buy a TV
that's already out the box.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.077
-Yep.

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:27.380
-You know there might be
something wrong with that TV.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.516
And they let you know,
"Hey, this is an open box.

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:31.851
We don't know.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.686
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.321
But it's only gonna cost $8."

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.657
And that's when you say,
"Let's go."

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.859
-So it would be sort of
a discount airline,

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.094
Let's Go Airlines.

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:42.629
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:44.463
Well, that will be
the working title.

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:46.666
I'm not sure if the FAA --

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.501
What I really want to call it
is just "Come On Then."

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.669
That's what I want to call it.

00:02:50.669 --> 00:02:52.505
But I'm not sure if that's
the right way to go.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.306
But, you know,
Southwest got everybody

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:56.975
straightened out eventually,
vouchers and all that.

00:02:56.975 --> 00:02:59.112
-Last time you were here,

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:00.580
you talked about
you got early COVID,

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.448
which you referred to
as whisper COVID.

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:04.083
-Yeah. That's when
you couldn't tell nobody.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.218
-Yeah.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:06.218 --> 00:03:09.088
-You get COVID and then
like three months later,

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.624
"You know I had it.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:14.660
I had it.
I just didn't say nothing."

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.729
You get COVID now,
you can just tell everybody.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:17.997
"Hey, you know
I got it right now!

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:20.199
What's going on?"
[ Imitates coughing ]

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:24.270
Just projectile cough
into strangers' faces.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.840
I don't -- I don't like
the restrictions of it, though.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.575
Like, I tried
to come to your show.

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:30.710
You had a live show.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.011
-I was doing stand-up in town,
yeah.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.746
-Yeah, and you shut it down.

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:37.116
And I got there and I was
a little perturbed.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.584
-Yeah.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:40.486
-'Cause at this point -- 'Cause
I've had COVID three times.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.222
What about my rights?
Like, I've...

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:45.090
done had it three times.

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:47.493
At this point, it should be
my choice if I want to --

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.261
Like, there should
just be an option --

00:03:49.261 --> 00:03:53.065
"Hey, somebody in this room
has COVID tonight.

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:56.002
Do you still want
to watch the show?"

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:57.537
And then I say, "Let's go!"

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:59.038
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.906
-I see a theme here.
I see a recurring theme.

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:02.308
-That's how you do it.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:05.144
Like, I don't like the fact
the government restrictions

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:07.213
take away my rights
to be stupid.

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:09.147
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.147 --> 00:04:10.349
That's all I'm saying.

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:11.651
-You have that right
just like anybody else.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.019
-We should have a COVID section
in restaurants.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:15.621
Remember smoking sections
in restaurants?

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:17.590
They should just have that
in the restaurant now.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.724
They already got the plastic.

00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:20.025
You got the little
outdoor porch.

00:04:20.025 --> 00:04:21.260
Put me out on the porch.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.128
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.128 --> 00:04:25.197
Everybody eating on the curb
and all of that [bleep]

00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:27.500
Just, "Hey, do you have COVID?"

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.469
"Yes, I do."

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:30.602
"Okay.
Well, here's your seat."

00:04:30.602 --> 00:04:32.505
"Thank you," and I can...

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:34.306
sit next to other people
with COVID.

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:36.275
I guess what I'm suggesting
is segregation.

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:38.578
-Oh, okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:40.746
Yeah, now that you say it, that
is what you've been describing.

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:42.281
-Let me backtrack on it
a little bit.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:44.316
I'm not sure --

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:48.053
I'm not sure if segregation
went so well the first time.

00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:51.156
-You -- Something else I've seen
you be very angry about

00:04:51.156 --> 00:04:52.959
